/target
plan.normalized.json
/.testagent/

# Claude Code local overrides. settings.json (shared, project-level) is NOT
# ignored -- only the per-machine layer and the backups /doctor writes.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.doctor-backup

# The observed-class histogram half of the residue-class evidence record: a
# property of the machine that ran the kill sampling, emitted on every test run
# (`PR5-CONF-004`). The declarations half, `effects/residue-classes.json`, IS
# checked in and IS compared byte-for-byte.
/effects/residue-histogram.json

# The T-ATTEMPT half of the observed-class histogram: the same machine-varying
# record as the line above, for the two capture commands `git add` and
# `write-tree`, written by the topology sampler on every test run.
/effects/attempt-residue-histogram.json

# Python bytecode. `scripts/` holds the parser the ready audit runs, and anything that IMPORTS it
# rather than running it leaves a `__pycache__` beside it -- so the rule is here as well as
# suppressed at the gate that drives it (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` in
# `.github/scripts/test-pr-ready-audit.sh`). A build artifact under an instrument path is not a file
# to clean up after; nothing should write it and nothing should be able to commit it. The rule is
# the fix and the artifact is only its first symptom, which is why this is here even though no
# invocation on this branch imports the parser.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
